/">Rohitashwa Ranjan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135033412,imgsize-756697.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[‘Should focus on actual criminals’: Dipke jabs police after shots fired at Tiger Shroff]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/should-focus-on-actual-criminals-dipke-jabs-police-after-shots-fired-at-tiger-shroff/articleshow/135033073.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135033073.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Abhijeet Dipke expressed his frustrations on social media regarding the recent shooting incident involving actor Tiger Shroff. The attack occurred while Shroff was leaving a birthday celebration in Mumbai, resulting in injuries to his driver and a fan. Three assailants on motorcycles fled the scene shortly after the incident. Police are investigating a social media post claiming responsibility for the attack and threatening others in the film industry.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/should-focus-on-actual-criminals-dipke-jabs-police-after-shots-fired-at-tiger-shroff/articleshow/135033073.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/should-focus-on-actual-criminals-dipke-jabs-police-after-shots-fired-at-tiger-shroff/articleshow/135033073.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-18T23:11:14+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Pranjal Pandey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135033221,imgsize-182808.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Barged in, cut power': AAP's Saurabh Bharadwaj claims Delhi Police harassing Bengali community in CR Park]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/barged-in-cut-power-aaps-saurabh-bharadwaj-claims-delhi-police-harassing-bengali-community-in-cr-park/articleshow/135031313.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135031313.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/barged-in-cut-power-aaps-saurabh-bharadwaj-claims-delhi-police-harassing-bengali-community-in-cr-park/articleshow/135031313.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/barged-in-cut-power-aaps-saurabh-bharadwaj-claims-delhi-police-harassing-bengali-community-in-cr-park/articleshow/135031313.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-18T22:45:20+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Subhadra Srivastava</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135032480,imgsize-231886.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Akshay Kumar meets Uttarakhand CM Pushkar Singh Dhami, discusses state’s film policy]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/akshay-kumar-meets-uttarakhand-cm-pushkar-singh-dhami-discusses-states-film-policy/articleshow/135032348.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135032348.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Akshay Kumar recently met Uttarakhand Chief Minister Pushkar Singh Dhami to discuss the state's film policy. The discussion aimed to identify ways to attract film productions and enhance local employment opportunities. During the meeting, Dhami highlighted the state's natural beauty and cultural heritage as advantages for filmmakers. Akshay is currently shooting a comedy film in Uttarakhand that features actor Raashii Khanna.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/akshay-kumar-meets-uttarakhand-cm-pushkar-singh-dhami-discusses-states-film-policy/articleshow/135032348.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/akshay-kumar-meets-uttarakhand-cm-pushkar-singh-dhami-discusses-states-film-policy/articleshow/135032348.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-18T22:39:49+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135032482,imgsize-140472.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Bimol Akoijam willing to contest Manipur Assembly polls if Congress offers ticket]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/bimol-akoijam-willing-to-contest-manipur-assembly-polls-if-congress-offers-ticket/articleshow/135031895.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135031895.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Congress MP Angomcha Bimol Akoijam expressed his willingness to contest in the upcoming Manipur Assembly elections. He stated his decision was for the future of the state and would respect the party's ticket offering. Akoijam currently faces serious allegations of sexual harassment and has been dismissed from Jawaharlal Nehru University. Multiple complaints from female students prompted a police investigation into his conduct and actions.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/bimol-akoijam-willing-to-contest-manipur-assembly-polls-if-congress-offers-ticket/articleshow/135031895.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/bimol-akoijam-willing-to-contest-manipur-assembly-polls-if-congress-offers-ticket/articleshow/135031895.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-18T22:17:50+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Yashasvi Vasistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135032034,imgsize-1413772.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Amit Shah to meet families of Punjab drug-trade victims on Oct 19, vows crackdown on ‘chitta’ trade]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/amit-shah-to-meet-families-of-punjab-drug-trade-victims-on-oct-19-vows-crackdown-on-chitta-trade/articleshow/135031872.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135031872.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Home Minister Amit Shah is scheduled to meet families affected by drug-related deaths in Punjab. Multiple incidents have highlighted the growing issue of 'chitta' trade in the state. Recent deaths involve a father of a drug addict and two anti-drug activists. Shah has criticized the Punjab government for its handling of the drug crisis and promised action.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/amit-shah-to-meet-families-of-punjab-drug-trade-victims-on-oct-19-vows-crackdown-on-chitta-trade/articleshow/135031872.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/amit-shah-to-meet-families-of-punjab-drug-trade-victims-on-oct-19-vows-crackdown-on-chitta-trade/articleshow/135031872.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-18T22:13:56+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Bharti Jain</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135031934,imgsize-28450.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Rajnath to represent India at SCO council of heads of govt meeting in Tajikistan today]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/rajnath-to-represent-india-at-sco-council-of-heads-of-govt-meeting-in-tajikistan-today/articleshow/135031776.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135031776.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/rajnath-to-represent-india-at-sco-council-of-heads-of-govt-meeting-in-tajikistan-today/articleshow/135031776.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/rajnath-to-represent-india-at-sco-council-of-heads-of-govt-meeting-in-tajikistan-today/articleshow/135031776.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-18T22:11:36+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Surendra Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135031912,imgsize-34956.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Global uranium production to dip by 50% by 2040 as demand set to double, says IAEA report; forecast could pinch India too]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/global-uranium-production-to-dip-by-50-by-2040-as-demand-set-to-double-says-iaea-report-forecast-could-pinch-india-too/articleshow/135031757.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135031757.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/global-uranium-production-to-dip-by-50-by-2040-as-demand-set-to-double-says-iaea-report-forecast-could-pinch-india-too/articleshow/135031757.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/global-uranium-production-to-dip-by-50-by-2040-as-demand-set-to-double-says-iaea-report-forecast-could-pinch-india-too/articleshow/135031757.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-18T22:10:51+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Surendra Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135031867,imgsize-183788.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Centre issues advisory to Meta, asks it to overhaul content promotion system on Facebook, Instagram]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/centre-issues-advisory-to-meta-asks-it-to-overhaul-content-promotion-system-on-facebook-instagram/articleshow/135031374.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135031374.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[The Centre has mandated Meta to ensure diverse recommendation algorithms for users on its platforms. The Ministry of Electronics and Information Technology released an advisory emphasizing due diligence under the IT Rules. It highlighted the need for rapid identification and review of content with public disturbance potential. Additionally, Meta must assist law enforcement agencies by providing necessary information promptly.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/centre-issues-advisory-to-meta-asks-it-to-overhaul-content-promotion-system-on-facebook-instagram/articleshow/135031374.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/centre-issues-advisory-to-meta-asks-it-to-overhaul-content-promotion-system-on-facebook-instagram/articleshow/135031374.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-18T22:07:31+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Karan Manral</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135031866,imgsize-91620.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Shots fired at Tiger Shroff, actor's driver hurt; Bishnoi gang claims responsibility - top developments]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/shots-fired-at-tiger-shroff-actors-driver-hurt-bishnoi-gang-claims-responsibility-top-developments/articleshow/135031464.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135031464.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/shots-fired-at-tiger-shroff-actors-driver-hurt-bishnoi-gang-claims-responsibility-top-developments/articleshow/135031464.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/shots-fired-at-tiger-shroff-actors-driver-hurt-bishnoi-gang-claims-responsibility-top-developments/articleshow/135031464.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-18T21:42:28+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rohitashwa Ranjan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135031482,imgsize-1697429.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[CJP's Dipke accuses state of delaying proceedings to prevent release of Saurav Das, Ashutosh Ranka]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/cjps-dipke-accuses-state-of-delaying-proceedings-to-prevent-release-of-saurav-das-ashutosh-ranka/articleshow/135030939.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135030939.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Abhijeet Dipke accused the state of deliberately prolonging the arrests of Saurav Das and Ashutosh Ranka. He claimed they are using delaying tactics to obstruct court proceedings and prevent their release. The Cockroach Janta Party plans to take legal action if the individuals are not released soon. CJP's legal head, Ratna Singh, criticized the Special Executive Magistrate for arbitrary behavior during the hearings.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/cjps-dipke-accuses-state-of-delaying-proceedings-to-prevent-release-of-saurav-das-ashutosh-ranka/articleshow/135030939.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/cjps-dipke-accuses-state-of-delaying-proceedings-to-prevent-release-of-saurav-das-ashutosh-ranka/articleshow/135030939.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-18T20:58:30+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Pranjal Pandey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135030939,imgsize-189594.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Attempts to weaken India's unity cannot be accepted': RSS leader Indresh Kumar on anti-SIR protests]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/attempts-to-weaken-indias-unity-cannot-be-accepted-rss-leader-indresh-kumar-on-anti-sir-protests/articleshow/135030949.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135030949.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/attempts-to-weaken-indias-unity-cannot-be-accepted-rss-leader-indresh-kumar-on-anti-sir-protests/articleshow/135030949.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/attempts-to-weaken-indias-unity-cannot-be-accepted-rss-leader-indresh-kumar-on-anti-sir-protests/articleshow/135030949.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-18T20:53:47+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Karan Manral</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135030999,imgsize-95544.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[CISF to reorganise eight territorial sectors into specialised functional units from November 1]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/cisf-to-reorganise-eight-territorial-sectors-into-specialised-functional-units-from-november-1/articleshow/135030596.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135030596.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Starting November 1, the Central Industrial Security Force will reorganize into functional sectors to enhance security management. This restructuring aims to address the specialized needs of various industries and government installations. Eleven sectors will be transformed to focus on specific sectors like coal, power, and petroleum. Existing arrangements for the Department of Atomic Energy and airports will remain unchanged. The move is expected to improve operational oversight and sector-specific expertise.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/cisf-to-reorganise-eight-territorial-sectors-into-specialised-functional-units-from-november-1/articleshow/135030596.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/cisf-to-reorganise-eight-territorial-sectors-into-specialised-functional-units-from-november-1/articleshow/135030596.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-18T20:23:33+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Bharti Jain</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135030613,imgsize-87930.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Nothing to do with Imran': MNS after Aamir Khan meets Raj Thackeray amid legal troubles for actor's nephew]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/nothing-to-do-with-imran-mns-after-aamir-khan-meets-raj-thackeray-amid-legal-troubles-for-actors-nephew/articleshow/135029597.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135029597.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/nothing-to-do-with-imran-mns-after-aamir-khan-meets-raj-thackeray-amid-legal-troubles-for-actors-nephew/articleshow/135029597.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/nothing-to-do-with-imran-mns-after-aamir-khan-meets-raj-thackeray-amid-legal-troubles-for-actors-nephew/articleshow/135029597.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-18T19:37:45+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Karan Manral</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135030327,imgsize-90280.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Evening news wrap: Rijiju alleges violence plot during protests, CM Suvendu orders probe into home guards after stampede &amp; more]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/evening-news-wrap-rijiju-alleges-violence-plot-during-protests-cm-suvendu-orders-probe-into-home-guards-after-stampede-more/articleshow/135029219.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135029219.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Kiren Rijiju alleged that opposition leaders are conspiring to incite violence amidst the Special Intensive Revision protests. West Bengal Chief Minister Suvendu Adhikari has ordered an investigation following a tragic stampede in Kolkata. Rahul Gandhi accused Prime Minister Narendra Modi and others of voter fraud while urging public support for Congress in upcoming elections.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/evening-news-wrap-rijiju-alleges-violence-plot-during-protests-cm-suvendu-orders-probe-into-home-guards-after-stampede-more/articleshow/135029219.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/evening-news-wrap-rijiju-alleges-violence-plot-during-protests-cm-suvendu-orders-probe-into-home-guards-after-stampede-more/articleshow/135029219.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-18T18:47:48+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Yashasvi Vasistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135029415,imgsize-832928.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Refrain from taking photos, take shelter': India advisory amid Houthi strikes in Saudi Arabia]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/refrain-from-taking-photos-take-shelter-india-advisory-amid-houthi-strikes-in-saudi-arabia/articleshow/135029150.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135029150.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/refrain-from-taking-photos-take-shelter-india-advisory-amid-houthi-strikes-in-saudi-arabia/articleshow/135029150.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/refrain-from-taking-photos-take-shelter-india-advisory-amid-houthi-strikes-in-saudi-arabia/articleshow/135029150.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-18T18:27:58+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rohitashwa Ranjan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135029184,imgsize-36434.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[‘What's the need for SSR?’ Akhilesh Yadav says BJP conspiring to add fake votes, urges SP workers to be vigilant]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/whats-the-need-for-ssr-akhilesh-yadav-says-bjp-conspiring-to-add-fake-votes-urges-sp-workers-to-be-vigilant/articleshow/135028835.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135028835.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Akhilesh Yadav has accused the BJP of manipulating electoral rolls by adding fake votes and deleting genuine votes. He urged party workers to remain vigilant at polling booths and defend against electoral malpractice. Yadav raised concerns over the Election Commission's rationale for revising electoral rolls, questioning the need for it. He also criticized the BJP government's performance on various issues impacting citizens, including education and corruption.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/whats-the-need-for-ssr-akhilesh-yadav-says-bjp-conspiring-to-add-fake-votes-urges-sp-workers-to-be-vigilant/articleshow/135028835.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/whats-the-need-for-ssr-akhilesh-yadav-says-bjp-conspiring-to-add-fake-votes-urges-sp-workers-to-be-vigilant/articleshow/135028835.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-18T18:10:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Yashasvi Vasistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https:/